 To demonstrate the utility of `r Biocpkg("curatedMetagenomicData")`, an example analysis is presented below. However, readers should know analysis is generally beyond the scope of `r Biocpkg("curatedMetagenomicData")` and the analysis presented here is for demonstration alone. It is best to consider the output of `r Biocpkg("curatedMetagenomicData")` as the input of analysis more than anything else.
 
+```{r, include = FALSE}
+# The example analysis relies on packages that are only in Suggests, so the
+# vignette has to build when they are absent -- R CMD check is allowed to run
+# without them. OmicsMLRepoR is unavailable on Bioconductor 3.24 right now
+# because it depends on rols, which was removed in that release.
+analysis_pkgs <- c("OmicsMLRepoR", "scater", "vegan", "lefser")
+have_pkg <- vapply(analysis_pkgs, requireNamespace, logical(1), quietly = TRUE)
+run_analysis <- all(have_pkg)
+knitr::opts_chunk$set(eval = run_analysis)
+```
+
+```{r, echo = FALSE, eval = TRUE, results = "asis"}
+if (!run_analysis) {
+    cat("**Note:** the example analysis below is shown but not evaluated,",
+        "because the following suggested packages are not installed:",
+        paste(analysis_pkgs[!have_pkg], collapse = ", "), "\n")
+}
+```
+
